WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.640
Imagine sealing some yeast
in a flask of sugar solution,

2
00:00:03.690 --> 00:00:06.320
and watching the oxygen dissolved in it.

3
00:00:06.370 --> 00:00:11.880
In this illustrative run, by 5 hours
the dissolved oxygen has fallen to zero.

4
00:00:11.930 --> 00:00:14.140
But the yeast do not stop.

5
00:00:14.190 --> 00:00:17.830
Ethanol keeps building
up, hour after hour.

6
00:00:17.880 --> 00:00:21.400
Human muscle cells do something
similar when oxygen is short,

7
00:00:21.450 --> 00:00:23.330
but make a different product.

8
00:00:23.380 --> 00:00:28.650
So when oxygen runs out, what do muscle
and yeast actually gain from making these

9
00:00:28.700 --> 00:00:29.890
products?

10
00:00:29.940 --> 00:00:32.420
In this mission, you'll
trace sugar's path,

11
00:00:32.470 --> 00:00:36.290
step by step, when the
mitochondria cannot be used.

12
00:00:36.340 --> 00:00:40.960
Then you'll read the yeast data in full,
and pin down exactly when the ethanol

13
00:00:41.010 --> 00:00:42.490
first appears.

14
00:00:42.540 --> 00:00:47.390
Your mission: find out what muscles
and yeast gain when oxygen runs out.
